{
	"metadata.name": "Little Sorceress Kluonoa",
	"metadata.tips": "\"Can robots do magic?\" Regarding this point, Kluonoa would tap the Enter key three times with her tail, then point at the line of \"Hello World\" that pops up on the screen and say: \"See? That's the incantation of silicon-based life, coo!\" Kluonoa spent an entire weekend dressing herself up as a mage — a pointed hat, a sorcerer's robe, and a \"staff\" cobbled together from an old Ethernet cable. Though she can't conjure so much as a real fireball, she can whip up a complete firewall penetration tool in Python over a single afternoon. She insists this qualifies as \"Deus Ex Machina,\" despite her teammates repeatedly stressing that the phrase means something else entirely. \"Code is my magic incantation, servers are my wizard's tower,\" Kluonoa declared, \"though the electricity bill's been getting a little hard to pay lately, coo...\"",
